From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] hwc2on1adapter: set displays the client has not revalidated

Every present makes the adapter set all displays in one HWC1 call, and
Display::set refuses a display that holds type changes the client has not
accepted. SurfaceFlinger validates and presents one display at a time,
so with two displays and a HAL that asks for client composition the other
display always has unaccepted changes, every set fails, and stale frames
reach the screen. Only require that the display was prepared; a display
the client has not revalidated keeps its previous client target.

---
diff --git a/graphics/composer/2.1/utils/hwc2on1adapter/HWC2On1Adapter.cpp b/graphics/composer/2.1/utils/hwc2on1adapter/HWC2On1Adapter.cpp
index 6a2253b..b3e494c 100644
--- a/graphics/composer/2.1/utils/hwc2on1adapter/HWC2On1Adapter.cpp
+++ b/graphics/composer/2.1/utils/hwc2on1adapter/HWC2On1Adapter.cpp
@@ -1272,7 +1272,10 @@ bool HWC2On1Adapter::Display::hasChanges() const {
 Error HWC2On1Adapter::Display::set(hwc_display_contents_1& hwcContents) {
     std::unique_lock<std::recursive_mutex> lock(mStateMutex);
 
-    if (!mChanges || (mChanges->getNumTypes() > 0)) {
+    // Every present sets all displays, and the client validates and presents
+    // them one at a time, so the others still hold type changes it has not
+    // accepted this round. They keep their previous client target.
+    if (!mChanges) {
         ALOGE("[%" PRIu64 "] set failed: not validated", mId);
         return Error::NotValidated;
     }
